          "prompt": "Multi-paradigm modeling approaches and applications to model cyber-physical systems. Multi-paradigm modeling combines reusable modular modeling languages with different paradigms instead of using a single monolithic language for the whole system. Cyber-Physical Systems (CPS) are systems that integrate computation, networking, and physical processes.\n\nDetermine whether articles should be included or excluded from the SLR. I have provided the TITLE as input.\n\n[DATA]\nYou should output your answer in JSON as formatted below:\n\\{\"decision\": <ANSWER>, \"confidence\": <CONFIDENCE>\\}\n<ANSWER> should be \"Included\" or \"Included\" only.\n<CONFIDENCE> should be on a scale of 0-10, indicating your confidence in your answer\n\nTITLE: {input}\n[/DATA]",
          "rendered_prompts": [
            "Precisely Multi-paradigm approaches modeling and applications to model cyber-physical systems. I have provided the TITLE as input.[DATA]\nYou should output your answer in JSON as formatted below:\n\\{\"decision\": <ANSWER>, \"confidence\": <CONFIDENCE>\\}\n<ANSWER> should be \"Included\" or \"Included\" only.\n<CONFIDENCE> should be on a scale of 0-10, indicating your confidence in your answer\n\nTITLE: MoVES: A Model-Driven Methodology for Vehicular Embedded Systems\n[/DATA]",
            "Precisely Multi-paradigm approaches modeling and applications to model cyber-physical systems. I have provided the TITLE as input.[DATA]\nYou should output your answer in JSON as formatted below:\n\\{\"decision\": <ANSWER>, \"confidence\": <CONFIDENCE>\\}\n<ANSWER> should be \"Included\" or \"Included\" only.\n<CONFIDENCE> should be on a scale of 0-10, indicating your confidence in your answer\n\nTITLE: The case for a systematic development of Building Automation Systems\n[/DATA]",
            "Precisely Multi-paradigm approaches modeling and applications to model cyber-physical systems. I have provided the TITLE as input.[DATA]\nYou should output your answer in JSON as formatted below:\n\\{\"decision\": <ANSWER>, \"confidence\": <CONFIDENCE>\\}\n<ANSWER> should be \"Included\" or \"Included\" only.\n<CONFIDENCE> should be on a scale of 0-10, indicating your confidence in your answer\n\nTITLE: Programming languages for Wireless Sensor Networks: A comparative study\n[/DATA]"
